    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The paring is something I've been being extra careful with, but it still feels like the wood is just fighting me at the very end. Even with the chisels being sharp enough to shave with, the fibers just seem to give way unpredictably. Is there any specific way to orient the wood or maybe use a backing board to support the fibers while I'm paring so they don't crush or blow out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
