      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To counteract the unpredictable fibers, try using a soft-faced paringBlake or marking gauge to stabilize the wood during the final stages of paring. This will help control the angle and reduce the impact on the fragile fibers. When securely holding the wood in place, you can also be more aggressive with side-to-side saw cuts on the waste, this loosens the stress on the fibers from an all-forward motion.",
